# Public project configuration. Copy to .env.local for local development.
# Both values are safe in the browser: the publishable key comes from the Supabase dashboard,
# Project Settings -> API Keys. For the local stack, use `eval "$(bash scripts/supabase/local-env.sh)"`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://wdcbbjvxrcxuaabcipqo.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Server-only secrets: set them in the private runtime (on Vercel as Sensitive, per environment),
# never in this file or the repository, and never with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY: the project's secret key (Project Settings -> API Keys). The call-back form
# (M5) stores requests with it; without it the contact page offers LINE and phone instead.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# GA4_PROPERTY_ID=
# EMAIL_USER=
# EMAIL_PASS=

# Meta Pixel and Conversions API (Facebook/Instagram ads), production domain only and only after
# the visitor agrees to advertising cookies; both off while unset. The dataset id is public.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
# META_CAPI_TOKEN: server-only (Events Manager -> the dataset -> Settings -> Conversions API ->
# Generate access token); set it on Vercel as Sensitive, never here.
# META_CAPI_TOKEN=
# META_CAPI_TEST_EVENT_CODE: optional, while checking events under Test events.
# META_CAPI_TEST_EVENT_CODE=
